{"task_id": "HumanEval/33", "solution": "def sort_third(l: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the indicies that are not divisible by three, while its values at the indicies that are divisible by three are equal\n    to the values of the corresponding indicies of l, but sorted.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not l:\n        return []\n\n    indices_to_sort = []\n    values_to_sort = []\n\n    # Identify elements at indices divisible by three and store them.\n    for i, val in enumerate(l):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            indices_to_sort.append(i)\n            values_to_sort.append(val)\n\n    # Sort the extracted elements in ascending order.\n    values_to_sort.sort()\n\n    # Create a shallow copy of the original list to modify.\n    result_list = list(l)\n\n    # Replace elements in the result list with the sorted values at their original positions.\n    for i, sorted_val in zip(indices_to_sort, values_to_sort):\n        result_list[i] = sorted_val\n\n    return result_list"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/33", "solution": "def sort_third(l: list):\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the indicies that are not divisible by three, while its values at the indicies that are divisible by three are equal\n    to the values of the corresponding indicies of l, but sorted.\n    >>> sort_third([1, 2, 3])\n    [1, 2, 3]\n    >>> sort_third([5, 6, 3, 4, 8, 9, 2])\n    [2, 6, 3, 4, 8, 9, 5]\n    \"\"\"\n    third_indices_values = []\n    for i, x in enumerate(l):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            third_indices_values.append(x)\n\n    third_indices_values.sort()\n\n    result = l[:]  # Create a shallow copy of the input list\n    sorted_idx = 0\n    for i in range(len(result)):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            result[i] = third_indices_values[sorted_idx]\n            sorted_idx += 1\n    return result"}
