{"task_id": "HumanEval/38", "solution": "def decode_cyclic(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Decodes a string encoded with a cyclic permutation.\n    This function reverses the transformation of 'abc' to 'bca', 'ab' to 'ba', and 'a' to 'a'.\n    \"\"\"\n    decoded_chars = []\n    n = len(s)\n    i = 0\n    while i < n:\n        if i + 2 < n:  # Block of 3: encoded 'xyz' -> original 'zxy'\n            # To get 'abc' from 'bca': original 'a' is at s[i+2], 'b' at s[i], 'c' at s[i+1]\n            decoded_chars.append(s[i+2])\n            decoded_chars.append(s[i])\n            decoded_chars.append(s[i+1])\n            i += 3\n        elif i + 1 < n:  # Block of 2: encoded 'xy' -> original 'yx'\n            # To get 'ab' from 'ba': original 'a' is at s[i+1], 'b' at s[i]\n            decoded_chars.append(s[i+1])\n            decoded_chars.append(s[i])\n            i += 2\n        else:  # Block of 1: encoded 'x' -> original 'x'\n            decoded_chars.append(s[i])\n            i += 1\n    return \"\".join(decoded_chars)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/40", "solution": "def triples_sum_to_zero(l: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if there are three distinct elements in the list that sum to zero.\n    Returns True if such a triplet exists, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(l)\n    if n < 3:\n        return False\n\n    # Sort the list to enable the two-pointer approach for efficiency.\n    sorted_l = sorted(l)\n\n    for i in range(n - 2):\n        # Skip duplicate elements for 'i' to avoid redundant calculations.\n        if i > 0 and sorted_l[i] == sorted_l[i - 1]:\n            continue\n\n        left, right = i + 1, n - 1\n        while left < right:\n            current_sum = sorted_l[i] + sorted_l[left] + sorted_l[right]\n\n            if current_sum == 0:\n                return True\n            elif current_sum < 0:\n                left += 1\n            else:  # current_sum > 0\n                right -= 1\n    return False"}
