{"task_id": "HumanEval/58", "solution": "def common(l1: list, l2: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Return sorted unique common elements for two lists.\n    >>> common([1, 4, 3, 34, 653, 2, 5], [5, 7, 1, 5, 9, 653, 121])\n    [1, 5, 653]\n    >>> common([5, 3, 2, 8], [3, 2])\n    [2, 3]\n\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Convert to sets for efficient intersection and uniqueness.\n    set1 = set(l1)\n    set2 = set(l2)\n\n    # Find common elements.\n    common_elements_set = set1.intersection(set2)\n\n    # Convert back to list and sort.\n    common_elements_list = list(common_elements_set)\n    common_elements_list.sort()\n\n    return common_elements_list"}
