{"task_id": "HumanEval/83", "solution": "def starts_one_ends(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a positive integer n, return the count of the numbers of n-digit\n    positive integers that start or end with 1.\n    This uses the principle of inclusion-exclusion: P(A or B) = P(A) + P(B) - P(A and B).\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Calculate count of n-digit numbers that start with 1\n    if n == 1:\n        count_starts_with_1 = 1 # Only '1'\n    else:\n        # First digit is 1 (fixed), remaining n-1 digits can be 0-9 (10 choices each)\n        count_starts_with_1 = 10**(n - 1)\n\n    # Calculate count of n-digit numbers that end with 1\n    if n == 1:\n        count_ends_with_1 = 1 # Only '1'\n    else:\n        # Last digit is 1 (fixed). First digit can be 1-9 (9 choices).\n        # Remaining n-2 digits (if n > 1) can be 0-9 (10 choices each).\n        count_ends_with_1 = 9 * (10**(n - 2))\n\n    # Calculate count of n-digit numbers that start AND end with 1\n    if n == 1:\n        count_starts_and_ends_with_1 = 1 # Only '1'\n    elif n == 2:\n        count_starts_and_ends_with_1 = 1 # Only '11'\n    else:\n        # First digit is 1 (fixed), last digit is 1 (fixed).\n        # Remaining n-2 digits can be 0-9 (10 choices each).\n        count_starts_and_ends_with_1 = 10**(n - 2)\n\n    total_count = count_starts_with_1 + count_ends_with_1 - count_starts_and_ends_with_1\n    return total_count"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/84", "solution": "def solve(N: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Given a positive integer N, return the total sum of its digits in binary.\"\"\"\n\n    def _calculate_sum_of_digits(number: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of decimal digits of a number.\"\"\"\n        total_sum = 0\n        s_num = str(number)\n        for digit_char in s_num:\n            total_sum += int(digit_char)\n        return total_sum\n\n    def _to_binary_string(number: int) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Converts a non-negative integer to its binary string representation.\"\"\"\n        if number == 0:\n            return \"0\"\n        return bin(number)[2:]\n\n    sum_of_digits = _calculate_sum_of_digits(N)\n    binary_string = _to_binary_string(sum_of_digits)\n    return binary_string"}
